Bugfix: Run occ from the server root when cron.php is called from the CLI

When cron.php was run from the command line it executed `./occ system:cron`
relative to the caller's working directory. A crontab line such as
`php -f /var/www/owncloud/cron.php` runs with the user's home as working
directory, so the shell could not find `./occ` and no background job ever ran,
without any error in the ownCloud log.

cron.php now invokes occ by its absolute path, with the same PHP binary.

https://github.com/owncloud/core/pull/41895
